KZ3 patch 1124 (SPU pass 105): upstream ps3recomp PR #481 by tekulvw (MIT), the SPU dispatch cache in front of
spu_lifted_lookup's full resolver, adapted: the cache lives in the spu_context (spu_context.dcache[512], 32-byte
entries, last in the struct) instead of upstream's __thread t_dcache[512] keyed by a per-context id.

Why in the context: patch 1017's rule, the MinGW toolchain emulates TLS (every thread-local read is a call into
__emutls_get_address, SPU pass 100); a context runs on one host thread at a time, so its entries need no atomics,
and spu_context_init zeroing the context replaces upstream's lifetime id. Keys as upstream: target, image, resident
overlay, resident task, registry count (now published with a release store after the entry is linked), and
dcache_residency, which spu_overlay_note_get bumps on every resident_code change. Misses are not cached.
SPU_DISPATCH_CACHE: unset/0 off (KZ3 default, upstream's is on), 1 on, 2 or "shadow" on with the full resolver run on
every hit, mismatches counted, the first 16 logged, the resolver's answer returned; shadow mode prints
"[spu-dcache] hits= misses= shadow_mismatches=" at every power of two from 1024 hits or misses, every 2^22 after, and at exit. The PR's dispatch-cache test case
runs with SPU_DISPATCH_CACHE=1 when the variable is unset. Tests: tools/spu/test_r105_dcache.sh (PR test 139/137
checks in all modes; tools/spu/test_r105_dcache.c: filled on one host thread, hit on another; default off; shadow
catches a stale entry). Note: KZ3's lifted code dispatches through spu_indirect_branch_mt's fast path (overlay,
then image, patch 1096's memo) first; this cache serves only the full resolver and the interpreter rejoin.
The array is not over-aligned: a first build with __attribute__((aligned(64))) hung K4 at start in 3 of 3 runs
(SPURS job manager spinning, RSX park not patched), the build without it ran (SPU pass 105; ASSUMPTION: MinGW GCC
does not realign the Win64 stack for over-aligned locals, and malloc'd contexts are 16-byte aligned).
Upstream candidate: the context-resident variant (no TLS).

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): ours (cache in the context, default off) over upstream's TLS cache (on by default upstream). TODO fixup: upstream's `dcache_id, dcache_residency` field in spu_context.h duplicates 1124's `dcache_residency` (compile error until removed).

